settings-display-help = Shown on sign-in pages and in this console; the name in URLs stays as it is.
settings-enabled-help = A disabled realm answers no logins and mints no tokens; the admin plane still works.
settings-self-registration-help = Opens the create-an-account door on the sign-in page. Off, the door is not there and accounts come from an administrator or a federation.
settings-email-as-username-help = Registration asks only for an address and keys the account on it. The name field disappears from the form.
settings-verify-email-help = A self-registered account is born owing the mailed verification, and registration answers check-your-mail even for an address already held, so who exists here stays unsaid. Needs email configured to actually send.
settings-login-with-email-help = The identifier field also accepts the account's address, when exactly one account holds it. An address two accounts share names neither, so allowing duplicate emails makes this door useless.
settings-reset-password-help = Shows the forgotten-password door on the sign-in page. Needs email to be configured to actually send the link.
settings-remember-me-help = Shows a keep-me-signed-in box on the sign-in page. Ticked, the session cookie survives the browser closing for the session's own lifespan; otherwise it dies with the window.
settings-client-registration-help = Whether applications may register themselves here, RFC 7591. Disabled hides the endpoint; open lets anyone; protected requires an initial access token.
settings-max-clients-help = How many clients self-registration may create, counted over what it created. Empty is no ceiling.
settings-requires-consent-help = A self-registered client was vetted by nobody, so each person consents before it gets anything.
settings-trusted-hosts-help = Redirect hosts a self-registered client may use. Open registration with no trusted hosts accepts any redirect target.
settings-access-lifespan-help = How long an access token stays valid, in seconds. Short is safer; clients renew with their refresh token.
settings-refresh-reuse-help = How many times one refresh token may be replayed before rotation refuses it. Zero refuses any reuse.
settings-offline-sliding-help = How long an offline grant may sleep between renewals, in seconds. Each renewal slides the window.
settings-offline-ceiling-help = The oldest an offline grant may get however often it renews, in seconds. Zero means the sliding window alone bounds it.
settings-offline-grants-help = How many live offline grants one person may hold across devices. Zero is no bound.
settings-refresh-rotation-help = Every renewal retires the refresh token it spent, so a stolen one dies at the owner's next renewal.
settings-require-par-help = Every authorization request must be pushed to the server first, RFC 9126, so the browser only ever carries a reference.
settings-agents-help = Whether this realm mints capability tokens for AI agents through the token exchange. Off, the surface refuses in its own words; agents themselves are clients with a registered capability root.
settings-ssl-help = Which requests must arrive over TLS. External spares private addresses; all refuses everything in the clear.
settings-privacy-door = Subject requests
settings-privacy-door-help = The realm's own privacy door: a person asks by mail, confirms by link, and the request lands in the register already verified.
settings-dsar-jurisdiction = Law
settings-dsar-closed = Door closed
settings-dsar-days = Response window (days)
settings-dsar-days-help = Your own deadline. Required where the chosen law fixes none; zero clears it.
settings-lockout-protected-help = Repeated failed sign-ins lock the account for a while, which is what stops a guessed password.
settings-lockout-failures-help = How many failures in a row before the account locks.
settings-lockout-first-help = How long the first lockout lasts, in seconds. It grows on further failures.
settings-lockout-ceiling-help = The longest a lockout may grow to, in seconds.
settings-lockout-reset-help = A quiet spell of this long forgets the failure count, in seconds.
settings-password-policy-help = What a new password must satisfy. Editing lands in a later slice; the document is shown as held.
mail-host-help = The SMTP relay that carries this realm's mail: reset links, magic links, verification.
